{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.BindingScalarKernelParityExclusion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingScalarKernelParityExclusion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingScalarKernelParityExclusion.kernel_coeff_existsUnique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingScalarKernelParityExclusion.kernel_coeff_existsUnique","kind":"theorem","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingScalarKernelParityExclusion.lean#L246-L269","doc":"**Exactly one new kernel coefficient per body order.** Matching the\ncoefficient of `x^{k+1}` in `G(qx) = R(q,x)·G(x)` expresses `(q^{k+1} − 1)·h_{k+1}`\nas `r_{k+1}·h_0` plus a tail involving only kernel coefficients of order `≤ k`.\nFor ANY body sequence with `h_0 ≠ 0` that equation has exactly one solution\n`r_{k+1}` — whatever the body terms are.\n\nSo kernel coefficients and body terms are in bijection, one for one: an\nunconstrained scalar ansatz is a **reparametrisation of the unknowns, not a\ndetermination of them**, and \"`ρ·A` is an output of the recursion\" is false as\nstated — the recursion transfers the unknown, it does not remove it. Every bit\nof the ansatz's content therefore lives in the FINITENESS of the Laurent window,\nwhich is precisely what `no_rational_riccati_solution` shows is unattainable in\nthe scalar form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingScalarKernelParityExclusion.no_scalar_kernel_on_carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingScalarKernelParityExclusion.no_scalar_kernel_on_carrier","kind":"theorem","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingScalarKernelParityExclusion.lean#L225-L238","doc":"**No scalar kernel on the carrier**, in the form the conjecture uses.\nA scalar kernel `R = P/Q` for a nonzero solution of `L_𝒦` is exactly a solution\nof the cleared q-Riccati identity below; that identity is unsatisfiable. So the\nrank-1 form of `prop:binding-genfun-qdifference` cannot hold on the carrier `𝒦`\nof `conj:qdifference-kernel-prolongation-symbol`, for ANY depth `d` — the depth\nnever enters the argument, only the degrees do. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingScalarKernelParityExclusion.no_rational_riccati_solution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingScalarKernelParityExclusion.no_rational_riccati_solution","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingScalarKernelParityExclusion.lean#L175-L223","doc":"**THE EXCLUSION.** For any field `K` and any `q ≠ 0, 1`, the cleared\nq-Riccati residual of `L_𝒦` is nonzero for every pair of nonzero polynomials.\nHence the q-Riccati has **no solution `a ∈ K(x)`**, so `L_𝒦` has no first-order\nright factor and the rank-2 module `𝒦` is irreducible.\n\nThe proof is the parity: by `riccati_degree_unique_max` exactly one of the three\nterms attains the top degree — the `PP` term (degree `1 + 2p`) when `u ≤ p`, the\n`QQ` term (degree `2u`) when `p < u` — and by `sub_sub_ne_zero_of_top_unique` a\nlone top-degree term cannot cancel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingScalarKernelParityExclusion.riccatiResidual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingScalarKernelParityExclusion.riccatiResidual","kind":"def","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingScalarKernelParityExclusion.lean#L166-L173","doc":"The cleared q-Riccati residual of `L_𝒦 = (q²x−1)σ² − (q−1)σ − (q−1)`.\nSubstituting `σy = a·y` with `a = P/Q` into `L_𝒦 y = 0` and multiplying through\nby `Q(qx)Q(x)` gives exactly this polynomial; `a` solves the Riccati iff the\nresidual vanishes. No coprimality of `P, Q` is needed anywhere below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingScalarKernelParityExclusion.dil_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingScalarKernelParityExclusion.dil_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingScalarKernelParityExclusion.lean#L157-L162","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingScalarKernelParityExclusion.natDegree_dil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingScalarKernelParityExclusion.natDegree_dil","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingScalarKernelParityExclusion.lean#L153-L155","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingScalarKernelParityExclusion.dil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingScalarKernelParityExclusion.dil","kind":"def","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingScalarKernelParityExclusion.lean#L148-L151","doc":"The q-dilation `(dil q P)(x) = P(qx)`, the substitution the shift `σ`\nperforms on a polynomial coefficient-wise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingScalarKernelParityExclusion.sub_sub_ne_zero_of_top_unique'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingScalarKernelParityExclusion.sub_sub_ne_zero_of_top_unique'","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingScalarKernelParityExclusion.lean#L133-L144","doc":"Mirror of `sub_sub_ne_zero_of_top_unique` for the case where the SUBTRACTED\ntail term `C` carries the top degree: its coefficient survives with a sign. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingScalarKernelParityExclusion.sub_sub_ne_zero_of_top_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingScalarKernelParityExclusion.sub_sub_ne_zero_of_top_unique","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingScalarKernelParityExclusion.lean#L120-L131","doc":"If `A` has degree exactly `M` and is nonzero while `B` and `C` sit strictly\nbelow `M`, then `A − B − C ≠ 0`: read off the coefficient at `M`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingScalarKernelParityExclusion.riccati_degree_unique_max","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingScalarKernelParityExclusion.riccati_degree_unique_max","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingScalarKernelParityExclusion.lean#L110-L116","doc":"**Unique strict maximum.** For every pair of degrees, exactly one of the\nthree cleared-Riccati terms attains the top degree: `T₁ = 1 + 2p` when `u ≤ p`,\nand `T₃ = 2u` when `p < u`. The middle term `T₂ = p + u` never wins. A lone\ntop-degree term has nothing to cancel against. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingScalarKernelParityExclusion.riccati_top_degrees_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingScalarKernelParityExclusion.riccati_top_degrees_ne","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingScalarKernelParityExclusion.lean#L104-L108","doc":"**The parity.** The `PP` term of the cleared q-Riccati has degree `1 + 2p`\nand the `QQ` term has degree `2u`; the first is odd-shaped and the second even,\nso they can never coincide. Equivalently `2u − 2p = 1` has no solution over ℤ.\nThis single fact is the Newton slope's denominator `2`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}